.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt BRUSH 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm brush
.Nd bash-compatible interactive shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl c Ar command
.Op Fl -rcfile Ar file
.Op Fl -input-backend Ar backend
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the RavenBSD interactive shell.
It is a Rust implementation of the Bourne-Again Shell language and is built from the
pinned MIT
.Sy brush
source.
It supports variables, quoting, functions, conditionals, loops, redirections,
command substitution, scripts and a bash-style
.Ev PS1 .
The RavenBSD image also keeps
.Pa /bin/rsh
as the rescue shell and
.Pa /bin/sh
as the POSIX shell.
.Sh PROMPT
The interactive prompt is
.Ev PS1 .
The RavenBSD
.Pa /etc/brush/brushrc
sets
.Ql \eu@\eh:\ew\e$
with the usual bash escapes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li \eu
The user name.
.It Li \eh
The host name.
.It Li \ew
The current working directory.
.It Li \e$
.Sq #
for root and
.Sq $
for other users, so the root prompt is distinct.
.El
The user@host and the final marker use the Raven Violet accent
.Pq #b388ff, xterm 183 ;
the cwd uses the path role
.Pq #f8f8f2, xterm 231 .
With
.Ev NO_COLOR
set, or
.Ev TERM=dumb ,
the prompt is the plain
.Ql user@host:cwd#/$
form with no escape sequences.
A non-interactive
.Fl c
command gets no prompt.
.Sh COMPLETION
Command and path completion are on by default through the bash-compatible
.Ic complete
and
.Ic compgen
builtins.
The RavenBSD rc adds
.Ql complete -W 'help exit' raven-test
as a calibration probe.
No foreign completion framework is loaded.
.Sh SHELL HISTORY
The rc sets
.Ev HISTFILE=/tmp/brush_history
(a writable ramfs path; the initfs is read-only),
.Ev HISTCONTROL=ignoreboth
(deduplicate entries and ignore leading-space commands),
.Ev HISTTIMEFORMAT='%F \&%T '
and
.Ev HISTSIZE=1000 .
The line editor's reverse search
.Pq Ctrl-R
searches the file.
A non-interactive
.Fl c
command neither reads nor writes history.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar command
Run
.Ar command
and exit.
No prompt or interactive history is loaded.
.It Fl i
Run interactively.
.It Fl -rcfile Ar file
Read the interactive startup file
.Ar file
instead of the default system and home rc files.
.It Fl -norc
Do not read any interactive rc file.
.It Fl -input-backend Ar backend
Select the line-editing backend:
.Ar reedline ,
.Ar basic ,
.Ar minimal
or
.Ar vt .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width HISTTIMEFORMAT -compact
.It Ev PS1
The prompt.
The RavenBSD rc sets the Raven Violet
.Sy user@host:cwd#/$
prompt described in
.Sx PROMPT .
.It Ev HISTFILE
History file path.
.It Ev HISTCONTROL
History deduplication policy; the RavenBSD rc sets
.Dq ignoreboth .
.It Ev HISTTIMEFORMAT
Timestamp format written to the history file.
.It Ev HISTSIZE
The number of commands kept in memory; the rc sets 1000.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Disable the prompt and tool colour.
.It Ev TERM
.Dq dumb
selects the plain prompt.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/brush/brushrc -compact
.It Pa /etc/brush/brushrc
RavenBSD interactive configuration: prompt, history and completion.
.It Pa /tmp/brush_history
The image-local history file selected by
.Ev HISTFILE
on the read-only initfs.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr raven 1 ,
.Xr rsh 1 ,
.Xr sh 1
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1 as the modern-shell profile's interactive shell.
.Sh BUGS
Interactive console input is still blocked on the target: the
.Ar minimal
backend hits the static-binary TLS destructor, the
.Ar basic
backend does not yet consume
.Pa tty:console
input, and
.Ar reedline
needs the multi-threaded tokio runtime, which static-binary threads do not
provide yet.
The
.Ar shell-test
profile keeps
.Xr rsh 1
as the working console shell until that platform work lands.
The
.Ar modern-shell
profile starts
.Nm
as the login shell; the rc, prompt, completion and history described here are
the configuration it loads, and the non-interactive
.Fl c
path is exercised by the
.Ar modern-shell
qtest while the interactive input backend work lands.
